      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Multiple giant aneurysms of the coronary arteries occur extremely rarely and are usually associated with Kawasaki disease in children. A 53-year-old man with multiple giant coronary artery aneurysms was treated successfully by aortocoronary bypass grafting."},
